  ORDER GRANTING SOUTWESTERN PUBLIC SERVICE COMPANY’S REQUEST
                            FOR CONFIDENTIAL TREATMENT


        THIS MATTER comes before Patrick C. Schaefer and Keven Gedko, hearing examiners

for the New Mexico Public Regulation Commission (“Commission”), upon the Request for

Confidential Treatment (“Request”) filed by Southwestern Public Service Company (“SPS”) for

its confidential Exhibit BR 3-1 (CONF), filed with the Commission on July 16, 2026. The Hearing

Examiners FIND AND CONCLUDE:

        1.      On February 24, 2026, Hearing Examiner Patrick C. Schaefer issued the Protective

Order in this case providing the rules and procedures governing the treatment of confidential

materials.

        2.      Decretal Paragraph L(3) of the Protective Order, which governs the confidential

treatment of documents provided pursuant to a Bench Request, requires a party seeking non-

disclosure of such documents to file a Request for Confidential Treatment with an accompanying

affidavit.

        3.      On July 15, 2026, during the public evidentiary hearing on the Comprehensive

Stipulation, Hearing Examiner Gedko asked SPS to provide, for tax credits earned from 2019

through 2025: (1) the tax-credit value generated by each resource; (2) the transfer costs associated

with credits SPS transferred; (3) the cash SPS received from those transfers; and (4) the related

remaining carryforwards. This was the Third Bench Request made at the Evidentiary Hearing.
                         BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Granting Southwestern Public Service Company’s             Docket No. 25-00079-UT
Request for Confidentiality


           4.       On July 16, 2026, SPS filed its Response to the Third Bench Request and

confidential Exhibit BR 3-1 (CONF). The Response contains an explanation of the information

provided and how the exhibit is organized, while Exhibit BR 3-1 (CONF) supplies the requested

values and supporting calculations.

           5.       On July 16, 2026, and in accordance with Paragraph L(3)(b) of the Protective

Order, SPS filed its Request for Confidential Treatment of Exhibit BR 3-1 (CONF). SPS there

asserts that the information provided in Exhibit BR 3-1 (CONF) is protected from disclosure under

the Commission’s Rules of Procedure, namely, Rule 1.2.2.8(B) NMAC, the Public Utility Act

(“PUA”), NMSA 1978, § 62-6-1 et seq., The Inspection of Public Records Act (“IPRA”), NMSA

1978, § 14-2-1 et seq., the Uniform Trade Secrets Act (“TSA”), NMSA 1978, § 57-3A-1 et seq.,

the Rules of Civil Procedure, Rule 1-026(C)(8) NMRA, and the Rules of Evidence, Rule 11-508

NMRA.1

           6.       In the Request, SPS also includes the affidavit of Ms. Naomi Koch, attached thereto

as Exhibit A, as required by Paragraph L(3)(b) of the Protective Order, and explains that the

information in Exhibit BR 3-1 (CONF), specifically, monthly PTC generation by wind resource,

transfer costs, cash received from transferred PTCs, PTCs carried forward or retained, and related

jurisdictional-allocation information is non-public market and transaction data that would allow

market participants to derive the prices and other economic terms at which SPS transferred PTCs.

The affidavit also explains that SPS takes reasonable steps to keep this information private and

that public disclosure would allow prospective buyers and sellers to use SPS’s transaction data to




